# Documentation

- Official product display name: **Orcan**. Technical ids stay lowercase (`orcan`, `ORCAN_*`).
- **Orcan** is the only product name in documentation — do not mention alternate or historical product names.
- **Cursor** means the Cursor editor / CLI — not the product.
- Docs are English-only under `docs/en/`. Keep user docs at B1–B2 and `README.md` short.
- Canonical AI map: root `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` (identical) + `docs/en/ai/project-context.md`.
- Public care / non-goals: `docs/en/llms.txt` via `scripts/repository/generate-llms-txt.py` (`make docs-llms`).
- Reflect CLI / Compose / config interface changes in `docs/` (and a one-line README pointer if needed).
- Do not document Make as the end-user interface; public API is `orcan` ([reference/cli.md](../../docs/en/reference/cli.md)). Maintainer `make dev-*` is documented under Testing / Makefile.
- Do not document commands that do not exist.
- Mark Docker socket risk with a warning.
- Prefer admonitions; link instead of duplicating long explanations.
- Before done: `make docs-check`.
